@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law s 2A (סעיף 2א, "מי שאינו תושב לענין החוק") and the residence words of s 65.
-- Row IL-33. Source lines 241-257 (s 2A), 803 (s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2)).
--
-- WHAT THE LAW SAYS. s 2A does not define a resident. It says, "among others", who is NOT regarded as one
-- "for the purposes of this Law": (b)(1) one present unlawfully; (2) the holder of a permit under the
-- Entry Order for residents of the Area; (3) a visitor (B/1 to B/4); (3A) a holder under regulation 5A;
-- (4) a holder of an A/1 temporary-residence visa and licence, in the periods (a) and (b); (5) a holder of
-- A/3 and a relative holding A/4; (c) a non-citizen holding another visa and licence for residence,
-- in the same two periods; (d) the Institute may regard an A/1 holder who is given an oleh visa within the
-- year as a resident from the day of the visa.
-- The Law has no positive test. This module therefore answers: is the person EXCLUDED by s 2A on the
-- day; and a person is an Israeli resident on the day if s 2A does not exclude him AND the case says he
-- lives in Israel (fork R1; `lives in Israel` is the one positive fact the case supplies).
--
-- FORKS. R3: whether "יושב בישראל" in s 65 is "תושב ישראל" in s 2A (nouns). R4: how exactly 183 days is
-- read (nouns). Both RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, default declined, declined
-- only where the readings differ.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 2A — who is not an Israeli resident`

§§ `The determining year`

-- "שנה" is twelve consecutive months (s 2A(a)). "השנה הקובעת" is the year that begins 183 days before the
-- day the visa and licence were granted.
-- src:244 | ”שנה“ – שנים עשר חודשים רצופים.
-- src:251 | (א) בשנה שתחילתה 183 ימים לפני יום מתן האשרה והרישיון כאמור (בסעיף זה – השנה הקובעת) – אם התגורר כדין בישראל פחות מ־183 ימים באותה שנה;
@ref NII s 2A(a), (b)(4)(a); lines 244, 251
GIVEN `the day granted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2A — the first day of the determining year of a visa granted on` `the day granted` MEANS
    `the day granted` MINUS 183

@ref NII s 2A(a), (b)(4)(a); lines 244, 251
GIVEN `the day`         IS A DATE
      `the day granted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — the day` `the day` `falls in the determining year of a visa granted on` `the day granted` MEANS
        `the day` AT LEAST first
    AND `the day` LESS THAN `add months` first 12
    WHERE first MEANS `s 2A — the first day of the determining year of a visa granted on` `the day granted`

§§ `The two limbs of (b)(4) and (c): fewer than 183 days, more than 183 days`

-- (a) the determining year itself, "if he lived lawfully in Israel fewer than 183 days in that year";
-- (b) the period before the visa day, "if he lived lawfully in Israel in the determining year more than
-- 183 days". Exactly 183 days falls under neither limb as the words read; the readings are kept by name.
-- src:251 | (א) בשנה שתחילתה 183 ימים לפני יום מתן האשרה והרישיון כאמור (בסעיף זה – השנה הקובעת) – אם התגורר כדין בישראל פחות מ־183 ימים באותה שנה;
-- src:252 | (ב) בתקופה שלפני יום מתן האשרה והרישיון כאמור – אם התגורר כדין בישראל בשנה הקובעת יותר מ־183 ימים;
GIVETH A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
`the reading this row takes of exactly 183 days in section 2A` MEANS
    `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`

@ref NII s 2A(b)(4)(a); lines 251
GIVEN r    IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — the holder lived lawfully fewer than 183 days, reading 183 as` r `:` days MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `183 days is counted with fewer than 183 days`  THEN days AT MOST 183
    WHEN `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`   THEN days LESS THAN 183
    WHEN `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read` THEN days LESS THAN 183
    WHEN `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ` THEN days LESS THAN 183

@ref NII s 2A(b)(4)(b); lines 252
GIVEN r    IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — the holder lived lawfully more than 183 days, reading 183 as` r `:` days MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `183 days is counted with fewer than 183 days`  THEN days GREATER THAN 183
    WHEN `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`   THEN days AT LEAST 183
    WHEN `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read` THEN days GREATER THAN 183
    WHEN `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ` THEN days GREATER THAN 183

§§ `Does the stay exclude residence on the day`

-- One limb pair for an A/1 holder and for (c)'s holder: excluded in the determining year if fewer than 183
-- days, and before the visa day if more than 183 days. An A/1 holder the Institute regards as a resident
-- from the day of the visa under (d) is not excluded from that day on; before it (b) still applies.
-- Everything is as on the day asked about; a reading that is not the declined one is applied as it is.
@ref NII s 2A(b)(4), (c), (d); lines 250-257
GIVEN `the day granted` IS A DATE
      days              IS A NUMBER
      `the day`         IS A DATE
      `from the day granted, regarded as a resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      r                 IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — a visa granted on` `the day granted` `, with` days `days lived lawfully in the determining year, excludes residence on` `the day` `, the Institute regarding the holder as a resident from the day granted:` `from the day granted, regarded as a resident` `, reading 183 as` r MEANS
        (   `s 2A — the day` `the day` `falls in the determining year of a visa granted on` `the day granted`
        AND `s 2A — the holder lived lawfully fewer than 183 days, reading 183 as` r `:` days
        AND NOT (`from the day granted, regarded as a resident` AND `the day` AT LEAST `the day granted`))
    OR  (   `the day` LESS THAN `the day granted`
        AND `s 2A — the holder lived lawfully more than 183 days, reading 183 as` r `:` days)

@ref NII s 2A(b), (c); lines 245-257
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      r         IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — the stay of` p `excludes residence on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER (p's residence)'s `permission to stay`
    WHEN `no permission that section 2A names` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `unlawful presence within section 13 of the Entry to Israel Law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a permit under the Entry to Israel Order (exemption of residents of Judea and Samaria, the Gaza Strip and northern Sinai, central Sinai, the Sharm el-Sheikh area and the Golan Heights), 5728-1968` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a visa and licence under regulation 5A of the Entry Regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a temporary-residence visa and licence of type A/1, under regulation 6(a) of the Entry Regulations` granted days decided THEN
        `s 2A — a visa granted on` granted `, with` days `days lived lawfully in the determining year, excludes residence on` `the day` `, the Institute regarding the holder as a resident from the day granted:` decided `, reading 183 as` r
    WHEN `a temporary-residence visa and licence of type A/3 (regulation 6(c)), or of type A/4 as a relative of the holder of A/3 (regulation 6(d)), of the Entry Regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another visa and licence for residence under the Entry to Israel Law, held by a person who is not an Israeli citizen, which section 2A(c) reaches` granted days THEN
        `s 2A — a visa granted on` granted `, with` days `days lived lawfully in the determining year, excludes residence on` `the day` `, the Institute regarding the holder as a resident from the day granted:` FALSE `, reading 183 as` r

-- The declined reading: evaluate under the three readings; answer if they agree, refuse if they differ.
@ref NII s 2A(b)(4), (c); Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      r         IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — the stay of` p `is judged to exclude residence on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `183 days is counted with fewer than 183 days`  THEN excludedFewer
    WHEN `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`   THEN excludedMore
    WHEN `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read` THEN excludedNeither
    WHEN `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ` THEN
        IF   excludedFewer EQUALS excludedMore AND excludedMore EQUALS excludedNeither
        THEN excludedNeither
        ELSE REFUSE "section 2A(b)(4) and (c) speak of fewer than 183 days and of more than 183 days; the holder lived exactly 183 days, and the text does not say which limb that is"
    WHERE
        excludedFewer   MEANS `s 2A — the stay of` p `excludes residence on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` `183 days is counted with fewer than 183 days`
        excludedMore    MEANS `s 2A — the stay of` p `excludes residence on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`
        excludedNeither MEANS `s 2A — the stay of` p `excludes residence on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read`

§§ `An Israeli resident`

-- Fork R1: a person is an Israeli resident on the day if s 2A does not exclude the stay and the case says
-- the person lives in Israel.
@ref NII s 2A(b), (c); fork R1
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      r         IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` r MEANS
        (p's residence)'s `lives in Israel`
    AND NOT `s 2A — the stay of` p `is judged to exclude residence on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` r

@ref NII s 2A; the ruling above
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` MEANS
    `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` `the reading this row takes of exactly 183 days in section 2A`

§§ `Section 65(a) "מבוטח" (2): one who sits in Israel (יושב בישראל)`

-- Fork R3: is "יושב בישראל" the "תושב ישראל" of s 2A? Reading 1: yes, so s 2A's exclusions apply. Reading 2:
-- no, it is the plain fact of living in Israel. They differ only for a person s 2A excludes who in fact
-- lives in Israel (a visitor who stays, a person present unlawfully): declined by default.
-- src:803 | (2) יחיד היושב בישראל, ואינו נעדר ממנה אלא העדר ארעי שהוא סביר, לדעת עובד המוסד שהוסמך לכך, ואין בו לסתור טענת אותו יחיד כי הוא יושב בישראל, ואינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
@ref NII s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2), line 803; s 2A; fork R3
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      r3        IS A `A reading of the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)`
      r4        IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` p `on` `the day` `, reading the words as` r3 `and 183 days as` r4 MEANS
    CONSIDER r3
    WHEN `sits in Israel is residence within section 2A` THEN asResident
    WHEN `sits in Israel is a matter of fact, whatever section 2A says` THEN asFact
    WHEN `the words sit in Israel are declined where section 2A would exclude a person who in fact lives in Israel` THEN
        IF   asFact
        THEN IF   asResident
             THEN TRUE
             ELSE REFUSE "section 65(a) says יושב בישראל (sits in Israel); section 2A says who is not a תושב ישראל (resident) for the purposes of the Law; the person lives in Israel but section 2A excludes the stay, and the text does not say whether the first words are the second"
        ELSE FALSE
    WHERE
        asResident MEANS `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` r4
        asFact     MEANS (p's residence)'s `lives in Israel`

@ref NII s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2); the ruling above
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` p `on` `the day` MEANS
    `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` p `on` `the day` `, reading the words as` `the reading this row takes of the words sits in Israel` `and 183 days as` `the reading this row takes of exactly 183 days in section 2A`

GIVETH A `A reading of the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)`
`the reading this row takes of the words sits in Israel` MEANS
    `the words sit in Israel are declined where section 2A would exclude a person who in fact lives in Israel`

-- The residence part of limb (2) as a whole: he "sits in Israel" and "is not absent from it except a temporary
-- absence that is reasonable, in the opinion of the Institute's employee authorised for it". That opinion is a
-- recorded determination (the residence facts' `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`),
-- not decided here. Row IL-06 takes the two as separate inputs (`resident in Israel`, `absent from Israel beyond
-- a reasonable temporary absence`); this is the pair they come from.
@ref NII s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2), line 803
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      r3        IS A `A reading of the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)`
      r4        IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(a) — lives in Israel as limb (2) requires:` p `on` `the day` `, reading the words as` r3 `and 183 days as` r4 MEANS
        NOT (p's residence)'s `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`
    AND `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` p `on` `the day` `, reading the words as` r3 `and 183 days as` r4
